.TH SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HAPTIC_AXES 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HAPTIC_AXES \- A variable containing a list of devices and their desired number of haptic (force feedback) enabled axis.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HAPTIC_AXES \(dqSDL_JOYSTICK_HAPTIC_AXES\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The format of the string is a comma separated list of USB VID/PID pairs in hexadecimal form plus the number of desired axes, e\[char46]g\[char46]
.PP
.BR 0xAAAA/0xBBBB/1,0xCCCC/0xDDDD/3
.PP
This hint supports a \(dqwildcard\(dq device that will set the number of haptic axes on all initialized haptic devices which were not defined explicitly in this hint\[char46]
.PP
.BR 0xFFFF/0xFFFF/1
.PP
This hint should be set before a controller is opened\[char46] The number of haptic axes won\(aqt exceed the number of real axes found on the device\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]5\[char46]

